# Root & Rise — environment variables
#
# Everything here is optional. The client falls back to the project the app
# ships against, so a checkout builds and runs without a .env file; set the
# VITE_ pair to point a build at a different Supabase project.
#
# The publishable key is public by design — it identifies the project in the
# browser and carries no privileges of its own. Row-level security on the
# project is what protects the data behind it.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Server-side, read by api/market on the host rather than compiled into the
# browser bundle. One token serves every reader. With it the market feed is
# OANDA's real-time CFD pricing — spot gold included; without it the public
# chart feed answers, delayed and with gold priced off the COMEX future. A
# practice-account token is free: register at oanda.com and mint one under
# Manage API Access. Set OANDA_ENV=live only for a token from a live account.
OANDA_API_TOKEN=
OANDA_ENV=

# Server-side, read by api/sweep. The sweep is the only author of the published
# record, so it writes under the service role rather than the publishable key -
# which is why this one is a secret and the VITE_ pair above is not. Set
# SUPABASE_URL alongside it when the host should sweep a different project than
# the browser bundle reads.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# What the scheduler proves it is with. One sweep costs a feed read of every
# swept instrument at every timeframe, so the endpoint answers nothing without
# it. Vercel sends it as a bearer token on its own cron invocations.
CRON_SECRET=

# Where the sweep reaches the market function. It resolves this from the
# request when the scheduler calls it, so this is only for driving a sweep from
# somewhere other than the deployment it should read.
SWEEP_ORIGIN=

# Where a newly published call is announced, so a setup that prints while the
# reader is driving still reaches them. The browser's own notifications only
# fire while a tab is open, which is the one case they are needed for. Any
# receiver that accepts a JSON post works - a Discord webhook URL reads the
# `content` field, most others read `text`, and both are sent. Leave it unset
# and the sweep announces nothing.
SIGNAL_WEBHOOK_URL=
